    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for elementwise tensor division. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradDivide" kindref="compound">GradDivide</ref> class represents the elementwise division operation in the computational graph, computing gradients for the quotient of two tensors. For the operation <formula id="23">$C = A / B$</formula> or equivalently <formula id="24">$C = A \oslash B$</formula> where <formula id="25">$\oslash$</formula> denotes elementwise division, the gradient computation follows from the derivatives:    <formula id="26">\[    \frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \frac{1}{B}, \quad \frac{\partial
C}{\partial B} = -\frac{A}{B^2}
\]</formula></para>
<para>During backpropagation, the incoming gradient  <formula id="8">$\frac{\partial L}{\partial
C}$</formula> is multiplied elementwise with the appropriate derivative according to the chain rule:    <formula id="27">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot
\frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \oslash B
\]</formula>     <formula id="28">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial B} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot
\frac{\partial C}{\partial B} = -\frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot
\frac{A}{B^2}
\]</formula></para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves copies of both input tensors as they are required to compute the gradients with respect to each input during the backward pass.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradDivideScalar" kindref="compound">GradDivideScalar</ref> for the gradient function for tensor-scalar division. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
